1
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:13,190
<i>Please stay safe, Rin, Shirou!</i>

2
00:01:45,670 --> 00:01:50,010
{\an4}Unlimited Blade Works

3
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:50,930
Is that all you have?

4
00:01:51,660 --> 00:01:54,190
As I thought, you were a fake.

5
00:01:54,190 --> 00:01:56,430
You are incapable of saving anything.

6
00:01:56,790 --> 00:02:00,390
That shabby Archer said as much, did he not?

7
00:02:00,390 --> 00:02:03,020
That your ideals were not your own.

8
00:02:03,020 --> 00:02:10,650
I'm astonished that a man without a thing to call his own
was arrogant enough to think he could accomplish anything.

9
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,910
"Champion of justice"?

10
00:02:13,220 --> 00:02:15,660
"A world where no one is hurt"?

11
00:02:15,660 --> 00:02:18,030
Don't be absurd.

12
00:02:18,030 --> 00:02:22,540
"Humanity" is the name for beasts that cannot find joy in life without sacrifice.

13
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:29,230
Your much-vaunted "equality" is nonsense spouted
by weaklings who cannot bear to stare into the abyss.

14
00:02:29,230 --> 00:02:32,760
It is naught but an excuse to cover up your own ugliness.

15
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:36,250
Yeah, he's exactly right.

16
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:39,590
My desires are borrowed.

17
00:02:39,590 --> 00:02:44,370
A pretense I put on, copied from someone I once saw saving another.

18
00:02:45,590 --> 00:02:48,690
When it happened, I was empty inside.

19
00:02:49,190 --> 00:02:51,320
Everyone was dying indiscriminately,

20
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:53,820
and nobody looked to save anyone else.

21
00:02:54,230 --> 00:02:57,330
If I hadn't resigned myself to the idea that that's how people are,

22
00:02:57,330 --> 00:03:00,200
I wouldn't have been able to keep on living.

23
00:03:01,590 --> 00:03:02,490
That's why...

24
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:08,380
That's precisely why I was inspired by his ideal.

25
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:10,600
Is that so wrong?

26
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:14,390
Are these feelings fake just because they aren't my own?

27
00:03:14,730 --> 00:03:17,760
Should I not achieve that ideal, just because it's fake?

28
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:20,100
No.

29
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:22,470
I know that's not right.

30
00:03:22,470 --> 00:03:25,700
It doesn't matter if it's fake. Or an unattainable wish.

31
00:03:26,620 --> 00:03:29,300
I know that I can't save everyone.

32
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:32,510
I know that no one can be saved without sacrifice!

33
00:03:34,550 --> 00:03:37,940
Even knowing that it was nothing but an ideal,

34
00:03:37,940 --> 00:03:40,430
I only chased after it even harder.

35
00:03:42,850 --> 00:03:45,890
Even if I hurt one to save many,

36
00:03:45,890 --> 00:03:50,090
I'll keep pursuing a happy future where no one will be hurt.

37
00:03:56,940 --> 00:04:00,600
And this is where that ideal ultimately lead him.

38
00:04:01,110 --> 00:04:07,600
A man once told me that what I believed in—
what I still believe in—was hypocrisy.

39
00:04:08,110 --> 00:04:09,330
But in spite of that,

40
00:04:09,330 --> 00:04:14,080
the man who said those words
stayed true to that same hypocrisy to the end.

41
00:04:14,630 --> 00:04:16,620
Which means that I can do it.

42
00:04:16,620 --> 00:04:20,120
Even if it's borrowed, even if it's fake, I don't care.

43
00:04:20,730 --> 00:04:22,610
I'm okay with that.

44
00:04:22,610 --> 00:04:26,620
Emiya Shirou can keep striving toward this dream!

45
00:04:27,150 --> 00:04:31,380
Even if he doesn't find a single thing he was searching for!

46
00:04:34,250 --> 00:04:35,630
Come on...

47
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:39,640
That's all there was to it?

48
00:04:41,270 --> 00:04:46,640
Though I may have held back,
I'm sure you felt the blast of wind from Ea.

49
00:04:46,970 --> 00:04:49,460
If you have all those weapons,

50
00:04:49,460 --> 00:04:52,020
why would you hold back just one?

51
00:04:52,020 --> 00:04:55,190
Only the supreme ruler may wield that blade.

52
00:04:55,190 --> 00:05:00,030
You haven't the right to so much as look upon it.

53
00:05:09,460 --> 00:05:11,060
Saber...

54
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:12,620
Are you unharmed, Shirou?

55
00:05:13,490 --> 00:05:15,420
I shall take over from here.

56
00:05:15,420 --> 00:05:19,680
No, you go help Tohsaka.

57
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:23,180
I can handle Gilgamesh by myself.

58
00:05:24,290 --> 00:05:26,330
What are you saying, Shirou?

59
00:05:26,330 --> 00:05:29,170
A mage is no match for a Servant.

60
00:05:29,170 --> 00:05:32,900
Yeah, but he and I are exceptions to the rules.

61
00:05:33,410 --> 00:05:34,650
Trust me.

62
00:05:34,980 --> 00:05:37,650
I know I can beat this guy!

63
00:05:47,210 --> 00:05:48,710
Good luck.

64
00:05:48,710 --> 00:05:51,230
I shall keep Rin safe.

65
00:05:51,230 --> 00:05:52,250
Saber...

66
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:58,550
I wasn't able to save you.

67
00:05:59,510 --> 00:06:03,140
I think that Grail isn't what you were hoping for.

68
00:06:03,660 --> 00:06:06,270
So take a good look.

69
00:06:06,270 --> 00:06:09,270
To make sure that you get it right next time.

70
00:06:09,820 --> 00:06:10,590
Shirou?

71
00:06:11,380 --> 00:06:14,280
Sorry, it's hard to explain.

72
00:06:14,280 --> 00:06:17,860
I guess I was never cut out to be your Master.

73
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:19,610
So...

74
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:21,950
That is untrue.

75
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:25,120
You are my Master, Shirou.

76
00:06:26,870 --> 00:06:30,120
I shall go fulfill my duty as a Servant.

77
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:33,250
Let us continue our discussion afterward.

78
00:06:51,850 --> 00:06:54,280
Are you mad, boy?

79
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:58,860
You choose to be the sacrificial pawn, rather than use Saber?

80
00:06:58,860 --> 00:07:00,510
You fool.

81
00:07:00,510 --> 00:07:05,020
The act of self-sacrifice is naught but a lie.

82
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:07,240
Being unable to see that, even now,

83
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:10,090
marks you as an incorrigible hypocrite.

84
00:07:11,370 --> 00:07:14,000
A fraud and a hypocrite, huh?

85
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:17,880
I guess. I am a fake through and through, after all.

86
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:20,970
But I was mistaken all along.

87
00:07:20,970 --> 00:07:24,260
My sword-making doesn't actually create them.

88
00:07:24,730 --> 00:07:27,010
There's only one thing that I can do.

89
00:07:27,010 --> 00:07:31,270
And that's to give form to what's in my mind.

90
00:07:31,850 --> 00:07:34,030
I am the bone of my sword!

91
00:07:34,770 --> 00:07:37,770
Steel is my body and fire is my blood

92
00:07:38,390 --> 00:07:40,780
I have created over a thousand blades

93
00:07:41,190 --> 00:07:43,030
Unaware of Loss,

94
00:07:43,220 --> 00:07:45,160
nor aware of Gain

95
00:07:45,760 --> 00:07:47,660
Withstood pain to create weapons,

96
00:07:48,090 --> 00:07:50,410
waiting for one’s arrival

97
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:54,160
I have no regrets. This is the only path

98
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:58,670
My whole life was Unlimited Blade Works!

99
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:14,420
That's right. I don't create swords.

100
00:08:14,420 --> 00:08:17,480
I create a world that contains an unlimited number of swords.

101
00:08:18,220 --> 00:08:21,980
That is the only magic allowed to Emiya Shirou.

102
00:08:22,610 --> 00:08:24,680
A Reality Marble, eh?

103
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:26,130
What of it?

104
00:08:26,130 --> 00:08:28,990
What can you do with this wretched mental landscape?

105
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:35,150
Don't be so surprised.

106
00:08:35,150 --> 00:08:37,630
Everything here is a fake.

107
00:08:37,630 --> 00:08:42,210
However, there's nothing that says a fake can't rival the real thing.

108
00:08:42,870 --> 00:08:45,400
If you say you're the genuine article,

109
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:49,130
then I'll just surpass everything about you and take you down.

110
00:08:50,510 --> 00:08:52,600
Here I come, King of Heroes.

111
00:08:53,430 --> 00:08:55,850
Do you have enough weapons in stock?

112
00:08:57,530 --> 00:09:00,480
You think too highly of yourself, mongrel.

113
00:09:02,300 --> 00:09:03,980
What in the world is that?

114
00:09:04,770 --> 00:09:09,090
Can being summoned incorrectly change a Servant so drastically?

115
00:09:11,740 --> 00:09:12,370
Rin!

116
00:09:12,730 --> 00:09:15,250
Where are you, Rin?

117
00:09:16,290 --> 00:09:17,250
Saber?

118
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:19,210
Rin!

119
00:09:19,210 --> 00:09:20,040
No, Saber!

120
00:09:21,820 --> 00:09:22,670
But...

121
00:09:23,020 --> 00:09:24,570
Trust me. Just don't.

122
00:09:24,570 --> 00:09:27,100
This muck is similar to a Servant in nature.

123
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:29,510
If you touched it, there's no telling what would happen.

124
00:09:30,750 --> 00:09:32,190
I understand.

125
00:09:32,190 --> 00:09:34,640
Then hurry to this side, Rin.

126
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:38,220
As long as you can get clear, I shall see to the rest.

127
00:09:38,220 --> 00:09:41,600
Yeah. Okay, I'll leave it to you.

128
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:45,030
But if I don't get there in time, do what has to be done.

129
00:09:45,740 --> 00:09:46,940
I cannot, Rin!

130
00:09:46,940 --> 00:09:49,820
If that is the alternative, I shall rescue you now!

131
00:09:50,270 --> 00:09:51,820
These curses are...

132
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:55,850
Rin! You used a Command Spell?

133
00:09:55,850 --> 00:09:57,440
Of course I did.

134
00:09:57,440 --> 00:10:02,580
I can't let the one person who can
destroy the Grail throw her life away.

135
00:10:03,090 --> 00:10:05,730
Besides, you don't need to worry about me.

136
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:08,630
I can get out of this, no problem.

137
00:10:08,630 --> 00:10:14,070
So don't worry about that.
Just believe in me and ready your holy sword.

138
00:10:14,070 --> 00:10:14,790
Rin...

139
00:10:15,260 --> 00:10:16,640
If only.

140
00:10:17,260 --> 00:10:20,390
This is definitely easier said than done.

141
00:10:20,390 --> 00:10:24,430
I wonder if this thing would let me go if I returned Shinji.

142
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:29,240
What's happening?

143
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:30,860
That's...

144
00:10:32,700 --> 00:10:33,530
Rin!

145
00:10:51,490 --> 00:10:52,880
Oh, no.

146
00:11:17,740 --> 00:11:20,320
Why are this mongrel's blades giving me pause?

147
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:22,000
Don't you get it?

148
00:11:22,330 --> 00:11:25,130
You may be ranked the highest of all Heroic Spirits

149
00:11:25,130 --> 00:11:28,730
because you possess over a thousand Noble Phantasms.

150
00:11:28,730 --> 00:11:32,590
But you're a king, not a warrior.

151
00:11:32,930 --> 00:11:37,100
You didn't choose the path of mastering a single Noble Phantasm.

152
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:39,930
You're like me: jack of all trades, master of none!

153
00:11:41,110 --> 00:11:46,320
When I'm done with you, there won't be a single bone shard left of your counterfeiting cranium!

154
00:11:53,590 --> 00:11:55,700
This is the pits.

155
00:11:55,700 --> 00:11:58,840
I can't even tell which way to go to get out of here.

156
00:12:02,380 --> 00:12:06,460
That jerk sure is using up my mana.

157
00:12:11,540 --> 00:12:13,710
This is it, I guess.

158
00:12:13,710 --> 00:12:16,890
But I won't let it end like this.

159
00:12:16,890 --> 00:12:18,720
By my Command Spell, I order you:

160
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:21,720
Saber, destroy the Holy Grail right now!

161
00:12:24,180 --> 00:12:26,310
What? Impossible!

162
00:12:26,660 --> 00:12:28,810
Rin! Get out of there!

163
00:12:29,230 --> 00:12:31,030
Sorry, Saber.

164
00:12:31,030 --> 00:12:34,590
You probably wouldn't do it if I just asked you, so I have to force you.

165
00:12:35,490 --> 00:12:38,570
And I guess I should apologize to you too.

166
00:12:39,310 --> 00:12:43,500
Sorry I couldn't save you, Shinji.

167
00:12:44,300 --> 00:12:47,210
Your pathetic whining offends me.

168
00:13:06,230 --> 00:13:07,500
Now go, Rin.

169
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:17,900
Hurry, Rin!

170
00:13:28,320 --> 00:13:29,420
Saber!

171
00:13:29,770 --> 00:13:32,840
I'm feeding you the last of my mana!

172
00:13:33,210 --> 00:13:35,840
So take that Holy Grail

173
00:13:36,260 --> 00:13:37,960
and blast it so hard

174
00:13:38,590 --> 00:13:40,640
there won't be a single trace left!

175
00:13:56,920 --> 00:13:58,280
Ex...

176
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:03,870
calibur!

177
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:45,030
Wow...

178
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:50,750
Our contract is concluded.

179
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:53,980
Victory is yours, Rin.

180
00:14:54,980 --> 00:14:58,770
Were it allowed, I would have liked to have remained to the end

181
00:14:58,770 --> 00:15:01,050
to see what becomes of you two.

182
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:05,040
However, that is not my role.

183
00:15:06,110 --> 00:15:09,130
After all, Shirou has you, Rin.

184
00:15:31,010 --> 00:15:32,330
Impossible!

185
00:15:32,330 --> 00:15:34,090
I'm being forced back?

186
00:15:34,090 --> 00:15:36,170
By a fraud like you?

187
00:15:36,170 --> 00:15:38,610
Against any other Servant,

188
00:15:38,610 --> 00:15:41,920
creating a world like this wouldn't let me hold my own.

189
00:15:41,920 --> 00:15:44,190
Having an unlimited number of swords

190
00:15:44,190 --> 00:15:47,430
wouldn't let me stand up to a Servant who had mastered one!

191
00:15:47,430 --> 00:15:49,510
But against you,

192
00:15:49,510 --> 00:15:52,310
my swords are ready and waiting,

193
00:15:52,310 --> 00:15:54,560
so I'm always one step ahead!

194
00:15:55,580 --> 00:15:57,060
D-Damn you...

195
00:15:57,730 --> 00:15:58,810
Damn you!

196
00:15:58,810 --> 00:16:00,050
Damn you! Damn you!

197
00:16:00,050 --> 00:16:01,030
Damn you!

198
00:16:06,250 --> 00:16:07,450
Damn you!

199
00:16:07,450 --> 00:16:11,700
To think that I must go all-out against the likes of you!

200
00:16:49,210 --> 00:16:50,990
Rho Aias.

201
00:17:13,890 --> 00:17:15,390
I shall grant you this:

202
00:17:15,770 --> 00:17:18,900
at this moment, you are powerful!

203
00:17:19,650 --> 00:17:22,650
You're not getting away!

204
00:17:53,990 --> 00:17:56,780
You ran out of mana? How anticlimactic.

205
00:17:57,520 --> 00:17:59,520
Victory is yours.

206
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:02,980
Die with that satisfaction, faker.

207
00:18:11,740 --> 00:18:12,700
What?

208
00:18:13,780 --> 00:18:16,330
Swallowing me accomplishes nothing...

209
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:18,910
Wait!

210
00:18:19,480 --> 00:18:21,900
The Holy Grail's hole?

211
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:27,800
That malformed abomination!

212
00:18:28,410 --> 00:18:32,470
Does it not know that a fellow Servant cannot be made its core?

213
00:18:32,470 --> 00:18:33,870
Damn...

214
00:18:33,870 --> 00:18:35,810
You're trying to take me down with you?

215
00:18:35,810 --> 00:18:37,160
Fool!

216
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:39,640
I haven't the least intention of dying!

217
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:41,770
Plant your heels, ruffian!

218
00:18:41,770 --> 00:18:44,230
At least until I climb back to where you are!

219
00:18:47,590 --> 00:18:48,820
As if!

220
00:18:49,370 --> 00:18:52,740
I'll rip off my own arm if that's what it takes!

221
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:58,240
Do so if you wish, but step to the right first.

222
00:18:59,750 --> 00:19:00,830
You—

223
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:06,400
Ar... cher...

224
00:19:22,760 --> 00:19:24,100
That guy...

225
00:19:24,640 --> 00:19:26,720
Always showing off.

226
00:19:36,740 --> 00:19:37,910
Archer!

227
00:19:47,320 --> 00:19:48,310
Archer...

228
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:52,300
It's unfortunate,

229
00:19:52,940 --> 00:19:54,640
but there you have it.

230
00:19:54,640 --> 00:19:57,510
Give up on the Grail this time, Rin.

231
00:20:04,200 --> 00:20:05,640
What's with that?

232
00:20:05,640 --> 00:20:08,670
This is hardly the time to be laughing!

233
00:20:08,670 --> 00:20:10,070
My apologies.

234
00:20:10,070 --> 00:20:13,600
I couldn't help it, given your state.

235
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:18,030
I was amused that you and I cut such sorry figures.

236
00:20:20,220 --> 00:20:24,040
Archer... Will you make a contract with me again?

237
00:20:26,480 --> 00:20:28,470
I can't do that.

238
00:20:28,470 --> 00:20:30,800
I doubt I have that right.

239
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:34,170
Besides, I no longer have a goal.

240
00:20:34,700 --> 00:20:38,070
My battle ends here.

241
00:20:38,070 --> 00:20:40,830
But... But this means you'll...

242
00:20:40,830 --> 00:20:44,430
No matter how much time passes, you'll never be saved.

243
00:20:47,110 --> 00:20:48,690
Oh, man.

244
00:20:49,700 --> 00:20:50,820
Rin.

245
00:20:52,040 --> 00:20:53,950
Look after me.

246
00:20:53,950 --> 00:20:56,930
As you know, I'm a bit hopeless.

247
00:20:56,930 --> 00:20:59,570
Give me a shoulder to lean on.

248
00:21:00,280 --> 00:21:01,530
Archer...

249
00:21:03,430 --> 00:21:05,560
Yeah, I know.

250
00:21:06,380 --> 00:21:08,330
I'll do my best.

251
00:21:08,330 --> 00:21:12,450
I'll try my hardest to make sure
he doesn't end up a twisted jerk like you.

252
00:21:12,450 --> 00:21:16,340
I'll make sure he learns to love himself!

253
00:21:16,340 --> 00:21:18,130
So you hang in there too!

254
00:21:19,550 --> 00:21:21,030
I have my answer.

255
00:21:22,150 --> 00:21:24,350
Don't worry, Tohsaka.

256
00:21:25,210 --> 00:21:28,290
I'll try my hardest from now on, too.

257
00:21:40,100 --> 00:21:44,300
Damn, I didn't even get the chance to tear him a new one.

258
00:21:50,440 --> 00:21:52,920
Let's go home, Tohsaka.

259
00:23:50,780 --> 00:23:53,910
Epilogue

260
00:23:50,780 --> 00:23:53,910
Next Time

261
00:23:50,780 --> 00:23:53,910
Next Time

262
00:23:50,780 --> 00:23:53,910
Next Time

